<BaseLayout title="About" description="Ancient China Wonder is an independent reader's project: a systematic, English-language universe of classical Chinese tales of the strange.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>An Independent Reader's Project</h1>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px;">
        <p>
          <strong>Ancient China Wonder</strong> exists because of a gap. The Chinese zhiguai tradition —
          two thousand years of ghosts, fox spirits, immortals, dragons and wonders — is one of the
          great fantasy literatures of the world. But outside the Chinese language it exists mostly as
          scattered translations: a story here, an anthology there, with no map connecting them.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site is an attempt at the map. It does three things that, as far as we know, no one else
          does together: it <strong>translates the stories</strong> from the public-domain originals;
          it builds the <strong>worldview</strong> they share — the realms, beings and rules — into a
          proper encyclopedia; and it writes the <strong>long essays</strong> that trace how the
          universe evolved. Every entry is cross-linked to the others, because the point is the
          connections.
        </p>

        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Original translations.</strong> Every rendering is made from the classical Chinese text and from nothing else. We do not adapt existing English translations.</li>
          <li><strong>Public domain only.</strong> All source texts are centuries old. No modern scholarly apparatus, no living authors' work, is used without permission.</li>
          <li><strong>Notes are original work.</strong> The cultural notes, encyclopedia entries and essays are written for this site, and are as important as the translations.</li>
          <li><strong>No tracking.</strong> No advertising cookies, no analytics beacons, no accounts. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Independent.</strong> This is a hobbyist site, not an academic institution, a publisher, or a government body.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>A note on method</h2>
        <p>
          Illustrations on this site are generated by AI in a unified ink-wash style and are always
          labelled as such. Translations condense the longest tales, and say so when they do. Errors,
          when found, are corrected publicly — the <a href="/translation-policy">translation policy</a>
          explains the working rules in detail.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Corrections, questions, suggestions for which story to translate next:
          see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Serious correspondence is read and answered.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Newsletter />
</BaseLayout>
